Object.assign(window.CONTENT, {policies: {"shipping-info":{"t":"Shipping Policy","html":"\n<section>\n\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t<span>Shipping Policy</span>\t\t\n\t\t<p>We ship throughout Canada and the United States, with delivery options for everything from small fixtures and accessories to oversized items such as vanities, bathtubs, sinks and appliances. Shipping methods and costs are determined by the size and weight of the product, delivery destination and any special delivery requirements.</p>\t\t\t</div>\n</section>\n<section>\n\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div><h3>Free standard shipping</h3><p>Free shipping across Canada &amp; USA on most orders: every item less than 70 lb ships free, however many you order.</p></div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div><h3>Freight delivery for large items</h3><p>Items of 70 lb or more and oversized pieces ship by freight delivery, curbside or driveway, with the cost confirmed before we process your order.</p></div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div><h3>2–5 day transit</h3><p>Most ground shipments arrive about 2–5 business days after leaving the showroom.</p></div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div><h3>Markham pickup</h3><p>Collect eligible orders from our Markham, Ontario showroom once we email that they’re ready.</p></div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n</section>\n\n<section>\n\t<div>\n\t\t</section>\n\n\t<div>\n\t\t\n\t\t<article><p>At Bath Emporium, we make shipping as simple and convenient as possible. We ship throughout Canada and the United States, with delivery options available for everything from small fixtures and accessories to oversized items such as vanities, bathtubs, sinks and appliances.</p><p>Shipping methods and costs are determined by the size and weight of the product, delivery destination and any special delivery requirements.</p><p>For shipping questions or assistance with a time-sensitive order, or outside of Canada and USA please contact us at (905) 944-0060 or info@bathemp.ca.</p><h2>Free Shipping</h2><p>We offer FREE standard shipping on eligible orders weighing less than 70 lbs within Canada and the United States.</p><p>Some exclusions may apply depending on the product, delivery location, manufacturer requirements or shipping method. Oversized products, remote-area deliveries and items requiring freight service may be subject to additional shipping charges.</p><p>If additional shipping charges apply to your order, our team will contact you before the order is processed.</p><h2>Standard Ground Shipping</h2><p>Most orders weighing less than 70 lbs are shipped by standard ground service.</p><p>Once your order has shipped, tracking information will be provided by email whenever available.</p><p>Most ground shipments arrive approximately 2–5 business days after leaving the showroom.</p><p>A signature is not normally required for small-parcel deliveries; however, signature requirements and final delivery procedures are determined by the shipping carrier and driver.</p><h2>Freight Delivery for Large &#038; Oversized Items</h2><p>Products weighing 70 lbs or more, as well as large or oversized products such as vanities, bathtubs, large sinks and certain appliances, may require freight delivery.</p><p>Unless otherwise arranged, standard freight delivery is curbside or driveway delivery only. It does not include bringing merchandise inside your home, garage, business or job site.</p><p>Someone must be available to receive and inspect the shipment. Freight carriers will typically contact the customer to arrange a delivery appointment, generally within a 2–4 hour window during regular business hours.</p><p>If the carrier is unable to contact the customer or complete a scheduled delivery, any additional storage, redelivery or return freight charges may be the customer&#8217;s responsibility.</p><p>For additional delivery requirements or questions, please contact our team before placing your order.</p><h2>Expedited Shipping</h2><p>Expedited shipping options may be available for select products, including Next Day, 2-Day and 3-Day service.</p><p>Please note that expedited shipping only reduces the carrier&#8217;s transit time after the product has shipped. It does not reduce manufacturer lead times, special-order production times or the time required to process an order before shipment.</p><p>Lead times shown on our website are estimates and should not be considered guaranteed ship or delivery dates.</p><p>Bath Emporium is not responsible for expedited shipping charges or other costs resulting from manufacturer, processing or lead-time delays.</p><p>For expedited shipping options, please contact Customer Service at (905) 944-0060 before placing your order.</p><h2>Local Markham Showroom Pickup</h2><p>Customers may choose to pick up eligible orders from our showroom in Markham, Ontario.</p><p>Once your order is ready, we will notify you by email with pickup instructions. Please wait until you have received confirmation that your order is ready before arriving for pickup.</p><p>Customers may also arrange for their own shipping company or carrier to collect merchandise with prior approval from Bath Emporium.</p><h2>Shipping &#038; Delivery Times</h2><h3>In-Stock Products</h3><p>Products shown as in stock typically ship within 2–5 business days from the date the order is placed.</p><p>Once shipped, most standard ground orders arrive within approximately 2–5 business days.</p><p>Products marked &#8220;In Stock&#8221; may include inventory physically available through Bath Emporium or inventory that a manufacturer or distributor has reported as available through a real-time inventory feed.</p><p>All inventory is subject to prior sale and availability.</p><h3>Products Not Currently in Stock</h3><p>Products that are not currently in stock typically require approximately 2 weeks before shipment; however, lead times vary by manufacturer and product.</p><p>Once the product ships, standard delivery is generally approximately 2–5 business days.</p><h3>Special-Order, Custom &#038; Made-to-Order Products</h3><p>Products that need to be specially ordered, produced or customized may have longer lead times.</p><p>Where available, we will provide an estimated lead time by email.</p><p>Because production schedules vary, we strongly recommend ordering custom and special-order products well in advance of your installation or project deadline.</p><h2>Backorders &#038; Inventory Changes</h2><p>We make every effort to provide accurate inventory information; however, availability can change quickly.</p><p>Occasionally, an item shown as available may sell before your order is processed or the manufacturer&#8217;s inventory may change.</p><p>If this occurs, we will notify you that the product is backordered. Depending on the circumstances, you may have the option to:</p><ul><li>Continue with the order and wait for the product;</li><li>Select an alternative product; or</li><li>Cancel the backordered item for a refund.</li></ul><h2>Approximate Shipping &#038; Lead Times</h2><p>We do our best to provide accurate shipping and lead-time estimates. However, all shipping, processing and delivery times are estimates only and are not guaranteed.</p><p>Manufacturer delays, inventory changes, production schedules, carrier delays, weather, customs and other circumstances outside our control may affect delivery.</p><p>Bath Emporium is not responsible for costs associated with shipping or delivery delays, including contractor charges, installation costs, labour charges or project delays.</p><p>We strongly recommend that customers do not schedule installation until all products have been received, inspected and confirmed to be correct and undamaged.</p><p>If you are working with a time-sensitive project, please contact our team at (905) 944-0060 before placing your order so we can help confirm current availability and estimated lead times.</p><h2>International Shipping</h2><p>For destinations outside Canada and the United States, please contact us at info@bathemp.ca or (905) 944-0060 for availability and a shipping quote.</p><p>International and cross-border shipments may be subject to customs clearance, tariffs, duties, brokerage fees, taxes and other import-related charges.</p><p>Unless otherwise stated, these additional charges are not included in the product or shipping price and are the responsibility of the customer.</p><p>Additional information may also be requested by the shipping carrier or customs authorities to complete customs clearance.</p></article>\n\t</div>\n\t"},"returns":{"t":"Return Policy","html":"\n<section>\n\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t<span>Return Policy</span>\n\t\t\n\t\t<p>At Bath Emporium, we want you to feel confident shopping for your home. We understand that sometimes a product may not be the right fit for your space, and our team is here to make the return process as straightforward as possible. Please review the policy below before starting a return.</p>\n\t\t\n\t</div>\n</section>\n\n<section>\n\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div><h3>14-day window</h3><p>Eligible products may be returned within 14 days of delivery.</p></div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div><h3>Unused &amp; boxed</h3><p>Unused, uninstalled and unassembled, in complete original packaging.</p></div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div><h3>Approval first</h3><p>All returns require approval from Bath Emporium before merchandise is shipped back.</p></div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div><h3>Restocking fee</h3><p>Approved returns are subject to a 25% restocking fee plus shipping.</p></div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n</section>\n\n<section>\n\t<div>\n\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t<span>To qualify for a return</span>\n\t\t\t<h2>Merchandise must be:</h2>\n\t\t\t<ul>\n\t\t\t\t<li>Unused, uninstalled and unassembled</li><li>In new and resalable condition</li><li>In its complete, original and undamaged manufacturer packaging</li><li>Complete with all parts, accessories, manuals and documentation</li><li>No writing on the packaging</li><li>Eligible for return under the applicable manufacturer’s return policy</li>\t\t\t</ul>\n\t\t\t<div><p>Products that have been installed, used, assembled or altered cannot be returned. Return eligibility and manufacturer policies may vary by product.</p></div>\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t<h2>Start a Return</h2>\n\t\t\t<p>All returns require approval from Bath Emporium before merchandise is shipped back. Once your request has been submitted, our customer care team will review it and provide return instructions if your item is eligible.</p>\n\t\t\t<p>Please have ready: order number, email address, product, reason for return, photos (if applicable) and your preferred resolution. <strong>Please do not ship merchandise back without authorization.</strong> Unauthorized returns may be refused.</p>\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t</div>\n</section>\n\n<section>\n\t<div>\n\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t<span>Need help before ordering?</span>\n\t\t\t<h2>Not sure about a finish, size or configuration?</h2>\n\t\t\t<p>We’re here to help before you place your order. Our product specialists can help you compare options, coordinate finishes and select products that work together, especially for larger kitchen, bathroom and whole-home projects.</p>\n\t\t\t<p></p>\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div><p>Return eligibility and manufacturer policies may vary by product. Nothing in this policy limits any rights or remedies available to customers under applicable consumer protection laws.</p></div>\n\t</div>\n</section>\n\n\t<div>\n\t\t\n\t\t<article><h2>Returns, Cancellations &amp; Damaged Items</h2>\n<p>At Bath Emporium, we want you to feel confident in your purchase. If your order arrives damaged, defective or incorrect, our team will work with you to resolve the issue as quickly as possible.</p>\n<p>Because many of the products we sell are fragile, oversized or specially ordered from manufacturers, it is important that all products are inspected immediately upon delivery and before installation.</p>\n<p>For assistance, please contact us at info@bathemp.ca or (905) 944-0060.</p>\n\n<h2>Damaged &amp; Defective Products</h2>\n<p>Although we take care to ensure products are properly shipped, merchandise may occasionally be damaged during transportation or arrive with a manufacturer defect.</p>\n<p>If this happens, Bath Emporium will work with you, the manufacturer and/or shipping carrier to help resolve the issue.</p>\n<p>To allow us to properly process a damage claim, customers are responsible for inspecting merchandise immediately upon delivery and reporting any damage within the required timeframe.</p>\n<p><strong>Please do not install a product that appears damaged, defective or incorrect.</strong></p>\n\n<h3>Small-parcel deliveries</h3>\n<p>If a small-parcel shipment arrives damaged, please do not automatically refuse the package.</p>\n<p>Accept the delivery and immediately photograph:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The outside of the shipping box;</li>\n<li>The shipping label;</li>\n<li>Any visible damage to the packaging;</li>\n<li>The damaged product; and</li>\n<li>The product model or identifying information, where applicable.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Please contact our Customer Service team immediately at (905) 944-0060.</p>\n<p>Shipping damage should be reported as soon as possible. Claims reported within 7 days of delivery may be submitted to the carrier; however, customers should notify Bath Emporium within one business day whenever possible to avoid delays or issues with a damage claim.</p>\n<p>Failure to report damage promptly may affect our ability to obtain a replacement or refund from the shipping carrier or manufacturer.</p>\n\n<h3>Large &amp; freight deliveries</h3>\n<p>Immediate inspection is especially important when receiving large products such as bathtubs, vanities and large sinks by freight carrier.</p>\n<p>Please inspect the shipment <strong>before signing</strong> the carrier&#8217;s delivery receipt or Bill of Lading.</p>\n<p>If there is any visible damage to the packaging or merchandise, even if it appears minor, clearly write &#8220;DAMAGED&#8221; and describe the damage on the Bill of Lading or delivery receipt before signing.</p>\n<p>We also strongly recommend taking photographs of the packaging and merchandise while the carrier is still present.</p>\n<p><strong>All freight damage must be reported to Bath Emporium within 24 hours of delivery.</strong></p>\n<p>If the product itself appears significantly damaged, you may refuse the delivery. Please contact Bath Emporium immediately if a shipment is refused so that we can anticipate the return and begin arranging a resolution.</p>\n<p>Customers who accept and sign for a freight delivery without noting visible damage may assume responsibility for damage that could have been documented at the time of delivery.</p>\n\n<h3>Damaged or defective product resolution</h3>\n<p>When merchandise is confirmed to have arrived damaged or defective, Bath Emporium will work with the customer to arrange the appropriate resolution, which may include repair, replacement parts or replacement of the product at no additional product cost.</p>\n<p>The exact resolution may depend on the nature of the issue and the applicable manufacturer&#8217;s warranty or carrier claim procedure.</p>\n<p>If a customer chooses to return an item rather than accept an available repair or replacement, the return may be treated as a standard customer return and applicable shipping and restocking charges may apply.</p>\n<p>Customers must follow the return or damage-claim instructions provided by Bath Emporium. Failure to follow the required procedure may result in additional charges, including charges associated with replacement merchandise.</p>\n<p>If a returned product is inspected and found to be in proper working condition and to have been shipped as ordered, the return may be treated as a standard customer return. The customer may choose to have the product shipped back at their expense or, where eligible, receive a refund subject to the applicable 25% restocking fee and shipping charges.</p>\n\n<h2>Cancellations</h2>\n<p>Please contact us as soon as possible if you need to cancel an order.</p>\n<p>Orders may be cancelled prior to shipment, delivery or pickup when possible. Any costs already incurred by Bath Emporium at the time of cancellation may be deducted from the refund.</p>\n<p><strong>Special-order, custom and made-to-order products cannot be cancelled or returned once the order has been placed with the manufacturer.</strong></p>\n<p>Orders cancelled after they have shipped or been made available for delivery or pickup will be treated as returns and will be subject to the applicable return policy, restocking fees and shipping charges.</p>\n<p>Approved cancellation refunds will be issued to the original purchaser and returned to the original method of payment.</p>\n\n<h2>Returns</h2>\n<p>All returns require prior authorization from Bath Emporium and are subject to a <strong>25% restocking fee plus shipping</strong>.</p>\n<p>Before returning any merchandise, please email info@bathemp.ca to request a Return Goods Authorization (RGA).</p>\n<p>Your email should include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Your name;</li>\n<li>Order number;</li>\n<li>Product being returned;</li>\n<li>Reason for the return; and</li>\n<li>Photos of the product and packaging, if requested.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Please wait until you have received written approval and an RGA number before shipping or returning merchandise.</p>\n<p>Returns sent without an RGA number may be refused, and any associated shipping or handling charges will be the responsibility of the sender.</p>\n<p>No return or credit will be processed without prior authorization.</p>\n\n<h3>Return period</h3>\n<p>Requests to return non-damaged Bath Emporium products must be submitted within <strong>14 days</strong> of receiving the merchandise.</p>\n<p>All merchandise must remain in perfect, unused and resalable condition with its original packaging.</p>\n\n<h3>Return condition requirements</h3>\n<p>To qualify for a return, merchandise must be:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>New, unused and uninstalled;</li>\n<li>In &#8220;new&#8221; or &#8220;like-new&#8221; condition;</li>\n<li>In its original, undamaged manufacturer&#8217;s packaging;</li>\n<li>In its original crating materials where applicable; and</li>\n<li>Complete with all original parts, accessories, product materials, manuals and instructions.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All returns are subject to inspection before a refund or credit is issued.</p>\n\n<h3>Non-returnable items</h3>\n<p>The following items cannot be returned:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Products that have been partially or completely installed;</li>\n<li>Products that have been assembled;</li>\n<li>Custom or made-to-order products;</li>\n<li>Special-order products;</li>\n<li>Discontinued products, unless confirmed to be defective;</li>\n<li>Floor models;</li>\n<li>Products identified as &#8220;Off Price,&#8221; clearance or similar;</li>\n<li>Products sold in a condition indicating they are not first-quality merchandise; and</li>\n<li>Products that no longer have their original packaging or cannot be resold in new condition.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Certain manufacturers may have additional return restrictions. Where applicable, manufacturer-specific return policies will also apply.</p>\n\n<h3>Restocking fees</h3>\n<p>Approved customer-requested returns are subject to a 25% restocking/re-handling fee, in accordance with applicable manufacturer policies.</p>\n<p>Original shipping charges and return shipping charges are non-refundable and will be deducted from the refund where applicable.</p>\n<p>If the return is required because of an error by Bath Emporium, confirmed shipping damage or a manufacturer-related issue that is not the customer&#8217;s responsibility, Bath Emporium will be responsible for the applicable return shipping costs.</p>\n\n<h3>Return shipping</h3>\n<p>Unless the return is due to an error by Bath Emporium, shipping damage or another issue not caused by the purchaser, the customer is responsible for:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Arranging the return carrier;</li>\n<li>Return shipping charges;</li>\n<li>Properly packaging the merchandise; and</li>\n<li>Insuring the shipment.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Approved returns must be shipped using insured ground transportation unless otherwise instructed by Bath Emporium.</p>\n<p>If Bath Emporium is responsible for the return shipping, the merchandise must still be shipped using the approved and most economical transportation method provided or arranged by us.</p>\n<p>For returns resulting from manufacturer error, shipping damage, an incorrect item or another issue not caused by the customer, Bath Emporium will provide instructions and, where applicable, arrange and pay for return freight and insurance.</p>\n\n<h3>Refused deliveries</h3>\n<p>Please do not refuse a delivery unless there is significant visible shipping damage or you have been instructed to do so by Bath Emporium.</p>\n<p>If a freight delivery is refused for any reason other than documented shipping damage or a shipping error by Bath Emporium, the shipment will be treated as a customer-requested return.</p>\n<p>Applicable return freight, original shipping charges, additional carrier charges and the 25% restocking fee may be deducted from the refund.</p>\n\n<h2>Refunds</h2>\n<p>All returned merchandise must first be received and fully inspected before a refund or replacement can be processed.</p>\n<p>Once the product has been inspected and confirmed to meet the applicable return requirements, the refund will be calculated based on the original product purchase price, less:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Applicable restocking or re-handling fees;</li>\n<li>Original shipping charges;</li>\n<li>Return shipping charges; and</li>\n<li>Any other applicable carrier charges.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Refunds will be issued to the original purchaser using the original method of payment.</p>\n<p>Credit card purchases will be refunded to the original credit card used for the purchase.</p>\n<p>Please allow additional processing time for your bank or payment provider to post the refund to your account.</p>\n\n<h2>U.S. Orders – Duties, Tariffs &amp; Customs Fees</h2>\n<p>For all orders shipped to the United States, customers are responsible for any applicable customs duties, tariffs, import taxes, brokerage fees, customs clearance charges, and other related expenses.</p>\n<p>This responsibility also applies to returns shipped back to Bath Emporium in Canada. Customers are responsible for all duties, tariffs, customs fees, and additional charges incurred when returning merchandise to Canada, including any charges assessed upon re-entry.</p>\n<p>Any customs-related charges billed to Bath Emporium for a return may be deducted from the customer&#8217;s refund. Original shipping charges, duties, tariffs, and customs fees are non-refundable.</p>\n<p>All returns must receive prior authorization from Bath Emporium and comply with our return policy and applicable laws.</p></article>\n\t</div>\n\t"},"privacy-policy":{"t":"Privacy & Cookie Policy","html":"\n<section>\n\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t<span>Privacy</span>\n\t\t\n\t\t<p>How we collect, use and protect your personal information, and the choices you have.</p>\n\t\t\n\t</div>\n</section>\n\t<div>\n\t\t\n\t\t<article><h2>Information We Collect</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>Information you give us:</strong> name, email, phone, shipping and billing address, order details, trade account and project information, messages and uploaded files.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Payment information:</strong> processed securely by our payment provider; we do not store full card numbers.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Automatic information:</strong> device, browser, pages viewed and cookies, as described below.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>How We Use It</h2>\r\n<p>To process and deliver orders, provide customer and trade support, respond to enquiries, prevent fraud, meet legal obligations and, with your consent, send marketing emails and improve our website.</p>\r\n<h2>Sharing</h2>\r\n<p>We share information only with service providers who help us run the business (payment processing, shipping carriers, manufacturers fulfilling your order, email and hosting services), and where required by law. Some providers may store information outside your province or country.</p>\r\n<h2>Cookies</h2>\r\n<p>Cookies are small files stored on your device. We use essential cookies without consent because the store can&#8217;t work without them. We only use analytics and marketing cookies if you allow them. You can change your choice at any time via .</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<tr><th>Category</th><td><b>Purpose</b></td><td><b>Consent</b></td></tr>\r\n<tr><th>Strictly necessary</th><td>Cart, checkout, login, security, currency selection, remembering your cookie choice</td><td>Always on</td></tr>\r\n<tr><th>Language (Google Translate)</th><td>Only if you choose a language other than English: loads Google Translate, which sets a <code>googtrans</code> cookie to remember your choice and sends page text to Google for translation</td><td>When you pick a language</td></tr>\r\n<tr><th>Analytics</th><td>Understanding site usage to improve it (e.g. Google Analytics)</td><td>Opt-in</td></tr>\r\n<tr><th>Marketing</th><td>Relevant advertising and measuring ad performance (e.g. Google Ads, Meta)</td><td>Opt-in</td></tr>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>We honour the Global Privacy Control (GPC) browser signal as a request to opt out of marketing cookies.</p>\r\n<h2>Your Rights</h2>\r\n<p>Under Canadian privacy law, you may request access to or correction of your personal information, and withdraw consent to its use, subject to legal limits. Quebec residents have additional rights under Law 25, including data portability and information about automated decisions. To make a request, email info@bathemp.ca or call (905) 944-0060.</p>\r\n<h2>US Residents</h2>\r\n<p>Depending on your state, you may have the right to know, access, correct and delete your personal information, and to opt out of its “sale” or “sharing” for targeted advertising. Use  or contact us. We will not discriminate against you for exercising these rights.</p>\r\n<h2>Retention &amp; Security</h2>\r\n<p>We keep personal information only as long as needed for the purposes above and our legal obligations, and protect it with appropriate safeguards.</p>\r\n<p>Last updated: October 7, 2026</p>\r\n</article>\n\t</div>\n\t"},"payment-methods":{"t":"Payment Methods & Security","html":"\n<section>\n\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t<span>Payment &amp; Security</span>\t\t\n\t\t<p>Pay by credit card, Apple Pay, Google Pay or PayPal at checkout. Every payment is processed by Stripe or PayPal over an encrypted connection; your card details never touch our servers.</p>\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t</div>\n</section>\n<section>\n\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div><h3>Credit &amp; debit cards</h3><p>Visa, Mastercard and American Express, charged in Canadian dollars when you place your order.</p></div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div><h3>Apple Pay, Google Pay &amp; Link</h3><p>One-tap express checkout on supported phones and browsers, with the card already saved to your device.</p></div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div><h3>PayPal</h3><p>Pay with your PayPal balance, bank account or a card through PayPal, including PayPal’s Pay Later options where PayPal offers them.</p></div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div><h3>Trade &amp; large orders</h3><p>Quotes, invoices and payment arrangements for trade accounts, projects and call-for-pricing items. Talk to our team.</p></div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n</section>\n\n<section>\n\t<div>\n\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t<span>Your payment is protected</span>\n\t\t\t<h2>How we keep your payment safe</h2>\n\t\t\t<ul>\n\t\t\t\t<li>Card payments are processed by Stripe and PayPal payments by PayPal, both certified to the highest level of the card industry’s security standard (PCI DSS Level 1)</li><li>Your card number is entered in the processor’s secure fields and is never stored on our servers</li><li>Every page of our store, including checkout, is encrypted (HTTPS)</li><li>Your bank may ask you to confirm the purchase (3-D Secure / Verified by Visa / Mastercard Identity Check) for extra protection</li><li>We never ask for your card details by email, phone or chat</li>\t\t\t</ul>\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div><p><strong>Need help with a payment?</strong> If a card is declined, you want to pay for a large order in instalments, or you need an invoice for a trade account, call us at (905) 944-0060 or email info@bathemp.ca. We’re happy to arrange it before you order.</p></div>\n\t</div>\n</section>\n\n\t<div>\n\t\t\n\t\t<article><h2>Accepted payment methods</h2>\n<p>You can pay for your order at checkout with any of the following. All payments are processed securely by Stripe or PayPal.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Credit and debit cards</strong> – Visa, Mastercard and American Express, processed by Stripe.</li>\n<li><strong>Apple Pay, Google Pay and Link</strong> – express checkout on supported phones, tablets and browsers, using the card already saved to your device or Link account.</li>\n<li><strong>PayPal</strong> – pay with your PayPal balance, a linked bank account or a card through PayPal. Where PayPal offers it, you can also choose PayPal&#8217;s Pay Later options at checkout; those are agreements between you and PayPal.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Cash on delivery, cheques and bank transfers are not available at checkout. If you are a trade customer or placing a large project order and need an invoice or another payment arrangement, please call us at <strong>(905) 944-0060</strong> or email info@bathemp.ca before ordering.</p>\n\n<h2>Currency and pricing</h2>\n<p>All prices on our website are in <strong>Canadian dollars (CAD)</strong>, and all orders are charged in Canadian dollars.</p>\n<p>You can display prices in US dollars using the currency menu at the top of the page. US-dollar prices are an estimate based on the current exchange rate and are shown for convenience only; the amount charged to your card or PayPal account is the Canadian-dollar total shown at checkout. Your card issuer or PayPal converts that amount at its own exchange rate and may apply a foreign-transaction fee.</p>\n<p>Products marked <strong>&#8220;Call for pricing&#8221;</strong> are quoted individually. Once you accept a quote, our team sends you a secure link or takes payment by phone, using the same payment methods.</p>\n\n<h2>Sales taxes</h2>\n<p>Prices are shown <strong>before tax</strong>. Taxes are calculated at checkout based on the <strong>shipping address</strong> and apply to products and shipping charges alike.</p>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Delivery province / territory</th><th>Tax applied at checkout</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Ontario</td><td>13% HST</td></tr>\n<tr><td>New Brunswick</td><td>15% HST</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Newfoundland and Labrador</td><td>15% HST</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Nova Scotia</td><td>14% HST</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Prince Edward Island</td><td>15% HST</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Alberta</td><td>5% GST</td></tr>\n<tr><td>British Columbia</td><td>5% GST, plus applicable PST</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Manitoba</td><td>5% GST, plus applicable RST</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Quebec</td><td>5% GST, plus applicable QST</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Saskatchewan</td><td>5% GST, plus applicable PST</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Northwest Territories</td><td>5% GST</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Nunavut</td><td>5% GST</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Yukon</td><td>5% GST</td></tr>\n<tr><td>United States</td><td>Canadian GST/HST generally does not apply to qualifying exports; applicable US sales taxes may apply</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>For deliveries to the United States, customs duties, tariffs, import taxes, brokerage fees and customs clearance charges, where they apply, are not included in the product or shipping price and are the responsibility of the customer. The same applies to returns shipped back to Canada, and such charges may be deducted from a refund. See U.S. Orders – Duties, Tariffs &amp; Customs Fees in our Shipping Policy.</p>\n\n<h2>When you are charged</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Your card or PayPal account is charged <strong>when you place the order</strong>, for the total shown at checkout, including any special-order or made-to-order items.</li>\n<li>If your order needs a freight quote, or additional shipping charges apply (oversized items, remote areas, special delivery requirements), our team contacts you to confirm the cost <strong>before the order is processed</strong>. Nothing further is charged without your agreement.</li>\n<li>Orders are not shipped, and special orders are not placed with the manufacturer, until payment has been received and verified.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Payment security</h2>\n<p>Card payments are processed by <strong>Stripe</strong> and PayPal payments by <strong>PayPal</strong>. Both are certified to the highest level of the payment card industry&#8217;s security standard (PCI DSS Level 1). Your card number is entered in the processor&#8217;s secure payment fields and is never stored on our servers; if you choose to save a card for next time, it is stored by Stripe, not by us.</p>\n<p>Our whole website, including checkout, uses an encrypted connection (HTTPS). To protect you against unauthorized use, your bank may ask you to confirm a purchase (3-D Secure, Verified by Visa or Mastercard Identity Check), and we may contact you to verify an order before it ships.</p>\n<p>Bath Emporium will never ask for your full card number, security code or online-banking details by email, phone or chat. If you receive such a request, please do not reply and let us know.</p>\n\n<h2>Refunds</h2>\n<p>Approved refunds are issued to the <strong>original purchaser</strong> and returned to the <strong>original method of payment</strong>: credit-card purchases are refunded to the card used, and PayPal purchases to the PayPal account. Please allow additional processing time for your bank or payment provider to post the refund to your account.</p>\n<p>Restocking fees, original shipping charges and return shipping charges may be deducted from a refund where they apply. See our Return Policy for the full details.</p>\n\n<h2>Trade accounts and large orders</h2>\n<p>Designers, builders, contractors and property managers can apply to our Trade Program. Once your application is reviewed, our team contacts you to set up your trade account and to discuss payment arrangements for projects and volume orders, including quotes and invoicing.</p>\n<p>For questions about any of the above, call <strong>(905) 944-0060</strong> or email info@bathemp.ca.</p>\n</article>\n\t</div>\n\t<section>\n\t<div>\n\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<details><summary>Which payment methods do you accept?</summary><div><p>Visa, Mastercard and American Express (through Stripe), Apple Pay, Google Pay and Link express checkout, and PayPal. Cash on delivery, cheques and bank transfers are not available at checkout; for trade accounts and large project orders, call us to arrange an invoice.</p>\n</div></details>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<details><summary>In which currency will I be charged?</summary><div><p>Bath Emporium accepts payments in both Canadian dollars (CAD) and US dollars (USD). You can select your preferred currency when shopping, and your order will be charged in the currency displayed at checkout.</p>\n</div></details>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<details><summary>When is my card charged?</summary><div><p>When you place the order, for the amount shown at checkout. If your order needs a freight quote or has extra shipping charges, we contact you to confirm before anything more is charged.</p>\n</div></details>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<details><summary>Are taxes included in the prices?</summary><div><p>Prices are displayed before tax. Canadian orders are subject to applicable GST, HST, PST, RST or QST, calculated based on the delivery province and added at checkout.</p>\n<p>US orders are tax-free, with no Canadian GST/HST or US sales tax charged.</p>\n</div></details>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<details><summary>Is it safe to pay on your website?</summary><div><p>Yes. Payments are processed by Stripe and PayPal over an encrypted connection and your card details are never stored on our servers. Your bank may ask you to confirm the purchase for extra protection.</p>\n</div></details>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<details><summary>How are refunds paid?</summary><div><p>Approved refunds go back to the original payment method, to the original purchaser. Allow a few business days for your bank or PayPal to post it. Restocking fees and shipping charges, where they apply, follow our Return Policy.</p>\n</div></details>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t</div>\n</section>\n"}}});
